{
  "_doc": "THE SHARED CATALOGUES of libs:ai: the Model Catalogue's subpages and the Task Catalogue, one data file read by every app that chats (Cloud Search, Cloud SuperIntel, Cloud Tools Small LLMs through AiChatPage; Cloud Code through tools/resolve-targets.py, which copies this file into targets.gen.json chat.catalogue). The Model button of the composer opens the whole Model Catalogue with the subpages in `tabs`: Frontier and Specialist are the declared lists below (ids are OpenRouter ids; the page marks one the live model list does not carry), Core is libs:model-catalogue's A Text / B Search / C Audio & Speech / D Visual Media tables (assets models/catalogue.json), Medium and Small are the chat rows of Cloud Tools' tools-models.json (`tools_models`, tier medium = 7B to 32B, small = at most 4B; a row with no openrouter_id runs only on the phone or the fleet Ollama and is shown greyed; test-tools-app.sh holds the copy in step with that file). The Task button opens the Task Catalogue: `tasks.groups`, each with categories of items. An item with agent and model declares its own mapping (a Big LLM task); an item with only id and label is a Medium & Small task whose mapping is ai-tasks.json (same id). Selecting a task greys Agent and Model and sets them from that mapping.",
